# shfl.idx of %tid.x from lane 0 in a 48x2 block: warps 1 and 2 each
# span both rows, and every lane of a warp stores at one address, one
# sector per warp. The tracer reads lane 0's %tid.x as
# 32 * floor(%tid.x / 32), so those warps read two addresses: the
# store's address is 128·⌊%tid.x/32⌋ + param_0, 1 to 2 sectors per warp
# request, ideal 1.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/shfl_2d_block.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [128·⌊%tid.x/32⌋ + param_0] sectors/req 1–2 (ideal 1){{$}}
